# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# Without this, a file's stored bytes depend on which machine committed it.
# Implementer units are dispatched into WSL against a Windows checkout: the
# working tree holds CRLF (core.autocrlf=true on the Windows side), WSL git does
# not convert on commit, and the blob lands with CRLF where it previously had
# LF. The result is a whole-file diff for a ten-line change — one unit reported
# 2136 lines changed when the real number was 328 — and a whole-file conflict on
# merge, as docs/DEPLOY.md produced.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text, then stores it with LF. Checkouts
# still get CRLF on Windows, so nothing changes for an editor on this machine.
* text=auto

# Binary, never converted. Corrupting these is silent.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.xlsx binary
*.xlsm binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.db binary
